indicators.caveats:
Data for ICBs are estimated from local authority data. In most cases ICBs are coterminous with local authorities, so the ICB figures are precise. In cases where local authorities cross ICB boundaries, the local authority data are proportionally split between ICBs, based on population located in each ICB.


The affected ICBs are:


o Bath and North East Somerset, Swindon and Wiltshire;


o Bedfordshire, Luton and Milton Keynes;


o Buckinghamshire, Oxfordshire and Berkshire West;


o Cambridgeshire and Peterborough;


o Frimley;


o Hampshire and Isle of Wight;


o Hertfordshire and West Essex;


o Humber and North Yorkshire;


o Lancashire and South Cumbria;


o Mid and South Essex;


o Norfolk and Waveney;


o North East and North Cumbria;


o Suffolk and North East Essex;


o Surrey Heartlands;


o Sussex;


o West Yorkshire.
